Keep a tilted DFT pen in range, and no button from the first frame in range

The position of a DFT pen was rejected when a neighbour of the strongest antenna was in antiphase
with it; with the Slim Pen 2 held at a strong tilt that is so for most frames (63 % in a capture
on the Surface Pro 9), so the pen kept dropping out of range. Such a neighbour now counts as no
signal on that side.

Each time the pen came back into range, the button state of the first frame was taken from the
phase of a signal far too weak to have one, before the MPP v2 binary window had decided: a
one-frame press of the barrel button (or a one-frame eraser). The magnitude based decision now
needs two frames in a row.

diff --git a/src/core/generic/dft.hpp b/src/core/generic/dft.hpp
index 3f42ed9..1fcca14 100644
--- a/src/core/generic/dft.hpp
+++ b/src/core/generic/dft.hpp
@@ -41,6 +41,10 @@ private:
 	// This is used instead of the button threshold detection.
 	std::optional<bool> m_mppv2_button_or_eraser = std::nullopt;
 
+	// What the magnitude based button detection saw in the previous frame.
+	bool m_button_candidate = false;
+	bool m_rubber_candidate = false;
+
 	// Boolean to track whether the pen is in contact according to mpp v2.
 	// This is used to override the contact state in the pressure frame handling.
 	std::optional<bool> m_mppv2_in_contact = std::nullopt;
@@ -243,6 +247,20 @@ private:
 			rubber = val > 0;
 		}
 
+		// Without a decision from the binary window the phase of a weak signal is
+		// all there is, and it is noise in the first frame after the pen came into
+		// range: a state counts once two frames in a row agree on it.
+		if (!m_mppv2_button_or_eraser.has_value()) {
+			const bool button_now = button;
+			const bool rubber_now = rubber;
+
+			button = button_now && m_button_candidate;
+			rubber = rubber_now && m_rubber_candidate;
+
+			m_button_candidate = button_now;
+			m_rubber_candidate = rubber_now;
+		}
+
 		m_stylus.button = button;
 		m_stylus.rubber = rubber;
 	}
@@ -438,6 +456,12 @@ private:
 			(sin * row.real.at(maxi + 1)) + (cos * row.imag.at(maxi + 1)),
 		};
 
+		// A neighbour that is in antiphase with the peak (a strongly tilted pen: the
+		// signal of the barrel leaks in on that side) is as good as no signal there.
+		// Without this the pen would drop out of range for as long as it is held so.
+		x[0] = std::max(x[0], 1.0);
+		x[2] = std::max(x[2], 1.0);
+
 		// convert the amplitudes into something we can fit a parabola to
 		for (u8 i = 0; i < 3; i++)
 			x.at(i) = std::pow(x.at(i), m_config.dft_position_exp);
@@ -570,6 +594,8 @@ private:
 
 		m_mppv2_in_contact = std::nullopt;
 		m_mppv2_button_or_eraser = std::nullopt;
+		m_button_candidate = false;
+		m_rubber_candidate = false;
 
 		m_tip_energy = std::nullopt;
 		m_zero_force_contact = false;
